infrastructure, which

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:00.390
is going to allow developers
to focus on their apps

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.250
while IT operations
teams can focus

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.019
on deployment and management.

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:06.240
And because containers
are so lightweight,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.944
individual services
can quickly be

00:01:07.944 --> 00:01:09.360
called when they're
needed and are

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.640
available almost immediately.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.740
HEATHER CROSS: Which
brings us to Kubernetes.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.600
Is a production
ready open source

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:18.150
platform and provides a
container centric management

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:18.976
environment.

00:01:18.976 --> 00:01:20.850
So instead of having
all of your applications

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.040
separate from your
libraries and your kernel,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.320
each application has its
own library associated

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.612
with it resting above a kernel.

00:01:27.612 --> 00:01:29.820
Kubernetes allows you to
interact with your container

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.190
cluster to deploy
and manage your apps,

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.490
perform administration tasks
and set policies, and monitor

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.170
the health of your
deployed workloads.

00:01:42.409 --> 00:01:43.950
